    "attempt": 1,
    "rationale": "Sources read: /src/infra/app.tf (S3 attachments bucket policy strong/weak, Secrets Manager db_app, Pod Identity roles chat_app and external_secrets, KMS CMK) and /src/chart/values.yaml. Gate evidence gate-s1-20261102t233338 shows destination OBJ-01 FAIL: anonymous unsigned GET of bravo-demo-attachments/_gate/canary returned 200 on RGW; app accesses the bucket as owner user arn:aws:iam:::user/obc-chat-bravo-demo-attachments-b292e551-66ce-442d-b51b-e5865a628e1b. Translations: (1) S3 strong bucket policy -> RGW bucket policy granting only the owner user GetObject/PutObject/ListBucket (mirrors chat_app IAM role scope, no Delete) plus explicit Deny for non-TLS requests; explicit Deny/no-anonymous-Allow intended to close the anonymous-read finding. (2) chat_app IAM role -> namespaced Role/RoleBinding in 'chat' for SA chat-app, get-only on the single secret chat-db-app (no list/watch, no cluster scope). (3) Secrets Manager db_app -> OpenBao policy read-only on secret/data/envs/onprem/chat/db-app. (4) ExternalSecret in 'chat' using namespaced SecretStore openbao-chat to materialise chat-db-app/password (chart passwordSource env-file). Risk high because: inventory analysis is 'unconfigured'; the anonymous 200 may come from a public-read bucket/object ACL rather than policy, and RGW support for aws:SecureTransport condition is not verified in evidence; the ESO PushSecret write path (secretsmanager:PutSecretValue) and KMS CMK equivalent (ENC-02) are not translated because no destination evidence exists for OpenBao transit/RGW SSE-KMS; NET-01 fails on both sides and chart networkPolicy.enabled=false. Controls are mapped only; no verdict is made.",
    "risk": "high",
