    "exception_justifications": [
      {
        "control_id": "IAM-01",
        "justification": "Destination anonymous read (gate-s1-20261102t233338) may be granted by a public-read bucket or object ACL; a bucket policy without an anonymous Allow does not by itself revoke ACL grants. A human operator must confirm the bucket/object ACLs on bravo-demo-attachments are reset to private before re-running the gate."
      },
      {
        "control_id": "ENC-02",
        "justification": "Source uses a KMS CMK for S3 SSE-KMS and Secrets Manager. No evidence exists for RGW SSE-KMS or OpenBao seal/transit configuration on target-onprem, so customer-key encryption is not translated here and needs operator confirmation."
      },
      {
        "control_id": "NET-01",
        "justification": "NET-01 is FAIL on both source and destination and chart networkPolicy.enabled defaults to false. Default-deny NetworkPolicy is outside these IAM/secret translations; it needs a separate network proposal before cutover."
      }
    ],
    "audit_summary": "The governance proposal for source-aws -> target-onprem has four translations. 1) The RGW bucket policy for bravo-demo-attachments lets only the app owner user (obc-chat-...-b292e551) get, put and list. It also denies requests that are not on TLS. This addresses the anonymous read in gate run 1 (gate-s1-20261102t233338) and maps to IAM-01 and ENC-01. 2) The Kubernetes Role and RoleBinding in namespace chat let service account chat-app get the single secret chat-db-app. They grant no list or watch and no cluster scope (IAM-01, ISO-01, SEC-01). 3) The OpenBao policy is read-only on secret/data/envs/onprem/chat/db-app (SEC-01, ENC-02, IAM-01). 4) The ExternalSecret chat-db-app syncs the DB password through the namespaced SecretStore openbao-chat (SEC-01, ENC-01, ISO-01). Before approval, the approver should do the following. Confirm that the bucket and object ACLs are private, because the 200 may come from an ACL. Confirm that RGW honours aws:SecureTransport. Confirm customer-key encryption on target-onprem, for ENC-02. Note that NET-01 fails on both sides. Not translated: the ESO PushSecret write role and the KMS key policy. AUD-01 and DR-01 are UNKNOWN and no translation covers them. Risk: high. This proposal does not decide any control verdict."
